# Stool Sentry

## Commit & Push

When the user says "Commit & Push", run the publish flow. Do not run it for any other commit. The Phase 1 handoff commit is an ordinary commit and must not follow this flow.

1. Do not change git config. If this machine has no commit identity, stop and ask.
2. Read version.properties. If origin already has the tag v{VERSION_NAME}, add 1 to the patch number and add 1 to VERSION_CODE. If that tag does not exist, publish the current version as-is. A hand-edited version such as 1.1.0 is kept when its tag is new. The first publish stays 1.0.0.
3. Commit the project. Do not commit Mailbox/, the keystore, keystore.properties, local.properties, or signing secrets.
4. Tag v{VERSION_NAME} and push the branch and the tag.
5. Wait until the Release GitHub Actions workflow for that tag succeeds. If it fails, do not bump again. Fix the build and re-run that same tag.
6. Write user-facing release notes with `gh release edit`. For v1.0.0, describe the first release. After that, describe the changes since the previous tag. Do not make another commit for the notes.
